From: 8CBdroid contributors
Subject: Omit microHAM discovery thread when glob is unavailable

finddevices is compiled only with glob support on POSIX. Its caller must use
the same condition. Android API 26 has no glob() and uses Android USB permissions
instead of scanning desktop /dev paths. No microHAM support is claimed.

--- a/src/microham.c
+++ b/src/microham.c
@@ -898,7 +898,7 @@
  */
 static void start_thread()
 {
-#if defined(HAVE_SOCKETPAIR) && defined(HAVE_SELECT)
+#if defined(HAVE_SOCKETPAIR) && defined(HAVE_SELECT) && defined(HAVE_GLOB_H)
     /*
      * Find a microHam device and open serial port to it.
      * If successful, create sockets for doing I/O from within hamlib
